  "scope": "Same 24 ordinary roots and search seeds as the first-continuation census and policy cost screen. Trace every tree choice, excluding rollouts. Replay each chosen joint action on a separate log-enabled battle and check exact physical state at subsequent choices and leaves. History remembers each own action and all new protocol lines at every decision boundary. Views also retain own complete state, field, opponent counters and hidden Quick Claw coin; loadout strata fix species, items, moves and stats. Depth counts joint decision transitions, not turns. Retain only views with at least two selected sets having 16 observations each within a loadout; the 32/64 thresholds are nested. Frozen UCB distributions come from final node visits/rewards reconstructed by trace and per-iteration backpropagation, or the actual shared first-continuation bandit. Uniform untried actions or a deterministic UCB maximum define each distribution. Comparisons concern retained encountered states, not full reachability or all information sets. Retrospective modes can differ under a common changing policy and must not quantify hidden-information dependence. Frozen policy differences establish structural dependence within matched histories, not value loss, optimality gaps, strength, or that more sharing is an improvement."
}
